  message: "Fixed in PR (dev 0046aeb9f4). Site-3's field-declarer walk (_walk_parents_for_field) used insertion-order BFS. On an uneven-depth diamond — E(C,D), C(B), where B and D both declare the same field name with divergent types — BFS returns D's field (direct base, hit first) while Python's real MRO [E,C,B,D] resolves it on B, so the inherited-field method bound to the wrong type. Fix: walk the _linearize_c3 MRO for src_lang=='python' (other languages keep BFS); an un-linearizable (cyclic/too-deep) Python hierarchy biases to unresolved (matches _walk_c3). Documented residual of WI-hiziz D1. Behavioral evidence: self.dep.run() in E resolves run on B's field type (BDep), not D's (DDep). Core package 100% coverage; 2 new tests (Red: the uneven-diamond resolves to DDep without the fix)."  # 7b8b
